	<!-- AoTv4 Combat Text window (CCustomWnd "AoTFctWnd"), opened by "/fct" or the AoT menu.

	     Controls the floating damage and healing numbers drawn in the world by core_floatingtext.
	     Everything here is a CLIENT display preference and is written to aotv4_floatingtext.ini in
	     the EQ folder, not to the server.  The one exception is the Healing toggle, which also tells
	     the server whether to send the FCTHEAL transport at all, because healing has no packet.

	     TWO ANCHORS, SPLIT BY DAMAGE vs HEALING.  Not by dealt vs taken, which is how every other
	     combat text mod splits them.  The question you are answering mid fight is "am I taking
	     damage" against "am I being healed", and the colour already tells you which way a number is
	     going.

	     Checkbox state is NOT read back off the widget.  CButtonWnd::SetCheck drives the visual, but
	     this build exposes no readable checked member, so the dll owns the state and pushes it out.
	     Same approach as the Zone Difficulty window's Port Group box.

	     Comments must never contain a double hyphen, which is illegal in XML and makes the SIDL
	     parser abort the WHOLE file, killing the client before character select.  Run
	     aotv4_client_install/validate_ui_xml.sh before copying this anywhere. -->

